{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"exegesis-stage","type":"group","x":0,"y":0,"width":540,"height":1280,"label":"1 · Biblical Exegesis","color":"#4A90D9"},
		{"id":"theology-stage","type":"group","x":600,"y":0,"width":540,"height":1280,"label":"2 · Theological Synthesis","color":"#9B72CF"},
		{"id":"formation-stage","type":"group","x":1200,"y":0,"width":540,"height":1280,"label":"3 · Formation Goals · proposed","color":"#65A86B"},
		{"id":"design-stage","type":"group","x":1800,"y":0,"width":540,"height":1280,"label":"4 · Session Design","color":"#D6B34B"},
		{"id":"production-stage","type":"group","x":2400,"y":0,"width":1140,"height":1280,"label":"5 · Resource Production · drafts awaiting Paul","color":"#9098A1"},
		{"id":"passage","type":"text","x":20,"y":50,"width":500,"height":340,"color":"#4A90D9","text":"# G01B · Galatians 1:10–24 CSB\nSecond study gathering. No book overview.\n\n1:10 · Not persuading or pleasing people; servant of Christ.\n1:11–12 · Gospel not of human origin; revelation of Jesus Christ.\n1:13–14 · Former zeal persecuted the church.\n1:15–17 · God called by grace and revealed his Son; Arabia, not an immediate Jerusalem consultation.\n1:18–24 · Limited contact; the churches glorified God."},
		{"id":"review-note","type":"text","x":20,"y":420,"width":500,"height":250,"color":"#4A90D9","text":"# Paul’s direction · opening\nReplace the Galatians overview with a short review of last session: Jesus gave himself to rescue; a different gospel adds a basis of acceptance besides Christ (1:1–9).\n\nDo not reteach the chapter map."},
		{"id":"source-record","type":"text","x":20,"y":700,"width":500,"height":360,"color":"#4A90D9","text":"# Sources actually read\nPhase 01 Canvas: Paul’s October 13 request.\nCSB 1:10–24 checked on Bible Gateway and Bible.com.\nKeller 2013 contents: chapter 2, “God’s Amazing Grace,” 1:10–24, p. 25. Questions not read.\nPeterson: no 1:10–24 excerpt. Freedom from people-pleasing is taught from verse 10.\n\nHandout questions are original until Keller’s bank is supplied."},
		{"id":"gospel","type":"text","x":620,"y":50,"width":500,"height":300,"color":"#9B72CF","text":"# Central idea\nGod gave this gospel by revealing his Son. Approval and religious achievement did not produce it. A life changed by grace leads the church to glorify God.\n\nApostolic revelation is not a model for private revelation today. Verse 17 is not a rule to avoid the church."},
		{"id":"boundaries","type":"text","x":620,"y":390,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"#9B72CF","text":"# Boundaries\nJewish identity and the law are not the enemy. Zeal can still oppose grace.\n\nTruth-telling is not harshness. People-pleasing is not the same as patience or love.\n\nNo new doctrine is claimed. Russ’s review is not required for this draft unless those boundaries are crossed."},
		{"id":"keller","type":"text","x":620,"y":710,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"#9B72CF","text":"# Keller and Peterson\nKeller remains the primary question source. This session uses his published passage cut only.\n\nPeterson stays secondary. His opening excerpt was not applied as a commentary on 1:10–24, and no quotation was written."},
		{"id":"mens-goals","type":"text","x":1220,"y":50,"width":500,"height":360,"color":"#65A86B","text":"# Men · proposed, awaiting Paul\nContinue Session 1: receive grace, and tell the truth instead of managing a competent image.\n\nBelonging: honesty does not require appearing hard to need.\nBeholding: God called Paul by grace and revealed his Son.\nBecoming: name one approval pressure; tell a brother one true thing."},
		{"id":"womens-goals","type":"text","x":1220,"y":450,"width":500,"height":360,"color":"#65A86B","text":"# Women · proposed, awaiting Paul\nContinue Session 1: identity in Christ’s grace, and encouragement without comparison.\n\nBelonging: welcome does not depend on the more admirable story.\nBeholding: the churches glorified God because of Paul.\nBecoming: give God the glory, and encourage a sister by noticing his grace."},
		{"id":"goals-review","type":"text","x":1220,"y":850,"width":500,"height":200,"color":"#65A86B","text":"# Not yet confirmed\nSession 1 angles were reviewed. These applications of them to 1:10–24 are proposals inside the workflow test. They are not universal claims about men or women."},
		{"id":"flow","type":"text","x":1820,"y":50,"width":500,"height":340,"color":"#D6B34B","text":"# 6:30–8:00 PM\n6:30–6:50 · Check-in\n6:50–7:10 · Block 1: short review + 1:10–14\n7:10–7:20 · Discussion 1\n7:20–7:40 · Block 2: 1:15–24\n7:40–7:50 · Discussion 2\n7:50–8:00 · Practice and prayer\n\nHandouts say Part 1 and Part 2."},
		{"id":"dates","type":"text","x":1820,"y":430,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"#D6B34B","text":"# Working dates\nMen’s Session 1: October 20, as Paul confirmed.\nWomen’s Session 1: October 27, moved by Paul.\nMen’s G01B: November 3.\nWomen’s G01B: November 10.\n\nG01B dates follow the next DEC-066 Tuesdays. They are not a full course calendar."},
		{"id":"discussion","type":"text","x":1820,"y":750,"width":500,"height":300,"color":"#D96B6B","text":"# Discussion · original, pending Keller\nTwo questions each part, from the text, adapted by Collective.\n\nMen: competence, record, telling a brother the truth.\nWomen: approval, comparison, encouraging a sister by giving God glory.\n\nDo not attribute these sentences to Keller or Peterson."},
		{"id":"production-status","type":"text","x":2420,"y":50,"width":500,"height":250,"color":"#9098A1","text":"# Export candidates · v0.1\nEditable masters and handouts in phase 03. PDFs are review candidates, not phase 04.\n\nCSB. Part 1/2. No timings or leader cues on the handout. Awaiting Paul’s review of synthesis, scripts, and pages."},
		{"id":"mens-draft","type":"file","x":2420,"y":340,"width":500,"height":220,"color":"#9098A1","file":"Groups Ministry/06 Resources/Curriculum Development/03 Develop Content/Collectives Galatians/Superseded — Twelve-Session Plan/Mens Galatians Session 2 Course Draft.md"},
		{"id":"womens-draft","type":"file","x":2420,"y":600,"width":500,"height":220,"color":"#9098A1","file":"Groups Ministry/06 Resources/Curriculum Development/03 Develop Content/Collectives Galatians/Superseded — Twelve-Session Plan/Womens Galatians Session 2 Course Draft.md"},
		{"id":"synthesis-file","type":"file","x":2420,"y":860,"width":500,"height":200,"color":"#9098A1","file":"Groups Ministry/06 Resources/Curriculum Development/02 Structure & Synthesize/Collectives Galatians/Session 2 Synthesis.md"},
		{"id":"mens-pdf","type":"file","x":3020,"y":340,"width":480,"height":220,"color":"#9098A1","file":"Groups Ministry/06 Resources/Curriculum Development/03 Develop Content/Collectives Galatians/Superseded — Twelve-Session Plan/Mens Galatians G01B 2026-11-03 Handout.pdf"},
		{"id":"womens-pdf","type":"file","x":3020,"y":600,"width":480,"height":220,"color":"#9098A1","file":"Groups Ministry/06 Resources/Curriculum Development/03 Develop Content/Collectives Galatians/Superseded — Twelve-Session Plan/Womens Galatians G01B 2026-11-10 Handout.pdf"}
	],
